Subject: media: i2c: vd55g1: power the VD55G0 off when it stops streaming

On the Surface Pro 12 (Intel) the rear OV13858 is a 4-lane link on CSI-2
port 0, which aggregates PHY 0 and PHY 1, and the VD55G0 IR sensor's
lane is on port 1, PHY 1. While the VD55G0 is powered, even in software
standby, the rear camera starts with both PHYs ready but never sees a
start of frame, and the ISYS stream stop and close time out.

After an IR stream the sensor stays powered for the 4 s autosuspend
delay, so opening the rear camera within that time failed every time
(0 s and 3 s after: no frames; 8 s and 15 s: fine). Suspend at once
when the VD55G0 stops streaming. IR then rear back to back now streams
on every attempt.
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g1.c b/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g1.c
index 72bb0d823719..65a5f2b5f8db 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g1.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g1.c
@@ -1305,7 +1305,13 @@ static int vd55g0_disable_streams(struct vd55g1 *sensor)
 	if (ret)
 		dev_warn(sensor->dev, "vd55g0 stream stop failed %d\n", ret);
 
-	pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(sensor->dev);
+	/*
+	 * On the Surface Pro 12 the rear camera's 4-lane link uses the PHY
+	 * this sensor's lane is on, and a powered VD55G0 keeps the rear
+	 * camera from starting. Power off now rather than after the
+	 * autosuspend delay.
+	 */
+	pm_runtime_put_sync_suspend(sensor->dev);
 
 	return ret;
 }
